| Deliberate, not a loophole: since `Log { ... }` is sugar for an object
| literal with "_class" prepended, it is structurally equal to any plain
| object literal that happens to have the same fields — there is no hidden
| tag distinguishing a "real" particle from a hand-written object that looks
| like one, and since equality goes by field name, not even the order of
| them has to match.
assert Log { x = 1 } = { _class = "Log", x = 1 }
assert Log { x = 1 } = { x = 1, _class = "Log" }
assert Log { x = 1 } ≠ Log { x = 2 }
assert Log { x = 1 } ≠ Warn { x = 1 }
